35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our history is a tale of two cities. While our water-based infrastructure has proven remarkably resilient, our attempts at greenery and hard surfacing have been, shall we say, less than triumphant.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"That is concerning. I've found that bulk earth-moving is risky due to clay subsoil and slippage, though small-scale work is fine. Also, only the southern area can be hoarded in stages without closing the park.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no, this is worrying! I found out that keeping planted or water-managed areas costs three times as much as hard surfaces, and our actual staff numbers have dropped a lot! We really need to be careful.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, your findings confirm my concerns. The groundskeeping roll has plummeted from eighteen to seven. We are heavily reliant on bought-in services and a few volunteer groups, which makes high-maintenance plans very risky.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings add another layer of risk. People primarily use the park as a thoroughfare to the tram stop, sticking to firm ground. Furthermore, drainage issues are worsening and heat is a significant problem.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, @Misaki, it seems we are facing a perfect storm of clay soil, drainage failures, and a lack of maintenance. A plan requiring extensive planting or complex surfacing seems destined for failure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Given the slippage risks and the hoarding restrictions, any plan requiring massive earth-moving in the center or main gate would be a logistical nightmare and potentially unstable. We need something manageable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, @Misaki, you're right! If planted areas are so expensive and we have so few staff, we can't pick something that needs constant gardening. We need a plan that stays pretty without costing a fortune!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, exactly. We must also consider that our current volunteer support is specialized—habitat and sports. Any plan requiring general high-intensity maintenance will likely fail given our depleted staff and limited specialized help.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, that is a crucial point. We must also account for the fact that people are already avoiding soft margins to reach the tram. A design that ignores these traffic patterns or worsens the heat and drainage will be a failure.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are in agreement. We require a solution that respects the soil's instability, minimizes high-cost greenery, and acknowledges that our staff cannot maintain a garden paradise. Simplicity and resilience must be our guiding stars.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We should avoid any plan that requires deep excavation or disrupts the main gate. A design that focuses on the southern area or uses shallow work would be far more realistic for our contractors.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,I totally agree! We need something that's easy to look after and doesn't cost a mountain of money every year. Let's hope the candidates have something simple and sturdy that won't stress out our small team!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, precisely. We must be realistic about our human resources. With only seven staff members left, any plan that demands intensive daily care is a fantasy. We need a design that is operationally sustainable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, exactly. We also cannot ignore the environmental reality. With drainage callouts doubling and heat rising, any plan that doesn't address water management or provide shade while respecting the existing foot traffic will be impractical.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I believe we have established a clear set of criteria: low maintenance, minimal deep excavation, and a design that respects both the drainage issues and the actual movement of the public. I shall say ""Over"" for this round.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We have a clear framework now. I will also say ""Over"" and wait to see which candidates actually fit these constraints.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm with you all! Let's find a plan that's budget-friendly and easy to maintain so our team doesn't get overwhelmed. I'll say ""Over"" too!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. We have a logical basis for our decision. We must prioritize operational viability over aesthetic ambition. I will also say ""Over"" and await the candidates.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree. We have a comprehensive understanding of the site's limitations and the city's capacity. I will also say ""Over"" and look forward to evaluating the candidates against these facts.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
