60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Looking at our findings, B is a disaster waiting to happen given our history with trees. A is too central for hoarding, and D is a maintenance trap. C, however, aligns with our resilient water infrastructure.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree about B; the slippage risk and main gate hoarding make it impractical. D is the most realistic for construction since it's in the south, but C addresses the drainage issues we found.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Wait, if planted and water areas cost three times as much as hard surfaces, isn't C really expensive to keep? A seems much cheaper to maintain and provides the shade Minako mentioned!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, A is problematic because it's in the center, which Misaki noted cannot be hoarded in stages. However, D is the most operationally viable; we already have volunteers for sports and it's in the south.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, @Mio, we must be careful. A's central location ignores the hoarding issue and the tram traffic. C addresses the drainage crisis and heat, but I worry about the maintenance costs Mio mentioned. D fits the site's logistics perfectly.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, @Asuka, you make a compelling case for D. While C is resilient, the upkeep costs Mio highlighted are a poison pill. D is logically sound: it's in the south and utilizes existing volunteer strengths.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Asuka"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, @Minako, I agree. D is the safest bet for construction. It avoids the clay slippage risks in the center and fits the hoarding constraints perfectly. It's the only plan that doesn't risk a logistical nightmare.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, @Misaki, if you're sure D is the easiest to build and we have volunteers to help, then I'm on board! I just want to make sure it won't be too expensive to maintain.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, D is the most sustainable choice. We have a dedicated volunteer group for youth league grounds, meaning the maintenance burden on our seven staff members is significantly reduced compared to the other options.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, that is the deciding factor. D respects the southern hoarding limits, avoids the clay risks in the center, and leverages existing volunteers. It is the most practical choice for the city's current capacity.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a rare and refreshing consensus. Plan D is the only option that survives the scrutiny of our logistical, financial, and operational constraints. I am fully in favor of the Sports Terraces.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Plan D is the only one that aligns with the contractor warnings and the site's physical constraints. It is the most responsible choice for the city. I vote for D.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm convinced! If it's the safest to build and we have volunteers to help out, it's the best way to keep the park great without overworking everyone. I vote for D too!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, exactly. Given the severe staffing shortages and the specific expertise of our current volunteers, Plan D is the only logically sustainable option. I vote for D.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, I agree. Plan D is the only one that balances the physical constraints of the land with the actual capacity of our people. It is the most realistic path forward. I vote for D.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we are all in agreement, I shall cast my final vote for Plan D. It is the only choice that prioritizes reality over rhetoric.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
